WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.5 · Financial Management
Cash flow, forecasting and runway

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Cash pays the bills: forecast it monthly, know your runway and set a trigger.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Forecast receipts and payments for twelve months.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Update with actual figures every month.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Decide in advance what you do below the trigger.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: cash falls below zero June to November; a US$15,000 seasonal loan, repaid in December, keeps the balance at US$3,700 or more.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a twelve-month cash forecast and a runway trigger.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
